<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Summon Fire</h1>
<p>Sphere: Summoning Sphere
Class: Conjurer (guild level 30)
Mana: 20
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre><a cmd='#'>cast summon fire</a>
tell elemental &lt;command&gt;
</pre>
<p>In a flash of fire and light, a small fire elemental (level 45) emerges to 
serve you, the strongest of the four elementals. It follows you, fights 
beside you when you are in a fight, and when your hit points drop below a 
third it tries to rescue you. You can give it orders with tell: to attack 
(tell elemental kill orc), to walk, and the like. It won't attack another 
player unless both of you have signed the Book of Blood.
</p><p>It can only stay on this plane a short time: from half a minute to a minute 
and a half, longer the better your magic and your skill in the spell. Then it vanishes in a 
puff of smoke, dropping whatever it carried. If it is killed first, it is 
gone too. You can have only one summoned servant at a time: summoning another 
sends the first one away.
</p><p>You must be standing, not fighting. It is also found on scrolls.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
